/*
Project: E-commerce Apache Web Server Log Onboarding

I use these SPL searches to validate Apache log ingestion
and investigate website errors.

These searches are examples for my portfolio project.
I will add test results after running them in my Splunk lab.
*/

-- 1. Verify data ingestion
-- I start by checking whether Apache logs are arriving
-- in the correct index and sourcetype.

index=web sourcetype=access_combined
| stats count by host, sourcetype


-- 2. Investigate HTTP errors
-- I check which HTTP errors are occurring most frequently.

index=web sourcetype=access_combined
| rex field=_raw "\"\s+(?<http_status>\d{3})\s+"
| where http_status>=400
| stats count by http_status
| sort -count


-- 3. Investigate checkout failures
-- I focus on checkout requests returning server errors.

index=web sourcetype=access_combined "/checkout"
| rex field=_raw "\"\s+(?<http_status>\d{3})\s+"
| where http_status>=500
| stats count by http_status


-- 4. Monitor website traffic
-- I review the number of requests over time.

index=web sourcetype=access_combined
| timechart span=5m count
